For the following C# code snippet: 
```cs
        if (ReturnValue >= 0)
        {
            Assert.AreGreater(ReturnValue, IndexOfXInOldList);
        }
```
The output of the converter tool would be:
```cs
        if (ReturnValue >= 0)
        {
            System.Diagnostics.Debug.Assert(ReturnValue >= IndexOfXInOldList);
        }
```
In the provided code, the comment ````If it is non negative, it is at least the index of x in old list ```` corresponds to the ````If the return value is non-negative, return value is at least the index of x in old list ```` comment starting with ````@@@ ```` in the given C# code. Hence, an ````Debug.Assert ```` statement is generated with the condition ````ReturnValue >= IndexOfXInOldList ````. Please note that the converter tool will need to use the proper names instead of common variable names such as ```ReturnValue``` and ```IndexOfXInOldList```, as those names are common placeholders and not actual variable name in this code snippet. Replace ```ReturnValue``` and ```IndexOfXInOldList``` by their actual names that are used in the real code.--------------------
